atlas fact-surfaces

# Generated from schemas/control/fact-surfaces.cue by
# cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tools/compile_fact_surfaces.sh. Do not edit.

architecture fact-surface-registry
  canonical_name FactSurfaceRegistry
  family surface
  domain Surface / Fact surfaces
  layer surface/web
  semantic_question Which fact an organ produces reaches which person, on which page, through which read?
  purpose One CUE registry names each produced fact, its producer, its read (a declared store and one bounded SELECT, or the declared route that already shows it), its audience and where it shows. One WebAddress renderer draws every page row at /x/<slug> inside the estate shell; /x lists every row the viewer may see.
  maturity implemented
  consumes PriceObservation
  consumes MerchantOffer
  consumes ProductIdentity
  consumes ItemFacet
  consumes RoleProgram
  consumes SourceChannel
  consumes SourceGap
  consumes SourceContributionReceipt
  consumes MatrixSubject
  consumes CanonicalDomain
  consumes LatentChart
  consumes NeighbourhoodSnapshot
  consumes CommerceStage
  consumes ResourceGrant
  consumes DeviceKey
  consumes DevicePairing
  consumes FeedAgentPolicy
  consumes CarrierSyncRequest
  consumes FieldDispatch
  consumes AccountActivityPresentation
  consumes GitHubAppConnection
  consumes ProviderCustomerAccount
  consumes ConnectionSourceCandidate
  consumes ReleaseApproval
  consumes ForeignOccurrence
  consumes SiteSearchIndex
  consumes SearchIndex
  consumes SearchPassage
  consumes StaticEmbeddingModel
  invariant every page row reads one declared store read-only through its declared lease, with one SELECT bound to a row limit, a progress deadline and a per-cell byte cap
  invariant public rows are only facts already public; member rows need a signed-in session; admin rows need the bonfyre admin grant /studio/admin checks
  invariant no row submits, publishes, pays or changes a record
  forbidden_inference a fact shown -> it is current, verified or the viewer may act on it
  forbidden_inference a fact listed in the registry -> that its producer is healthy or still running
  forbidden_inference an empty surface -> that the producer has nothing; the store may be absent on this host
  known_gap a fact whose producer writes no store WebAddress may open (files, JSON receipts, stores absent on this host) has no row; tools/compile_fact_surfaces.sh lists none of them
  source_path schemas/control/fact-surfaces.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tools/compile_fact_surfaces.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/fact_surface_web.h
  source_path schemas/storage/stores/cmd-BonfyreAdmission.cue
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/fact_surfaces_test.sh builds stores from nothing, shows a public row to anyone, sends a signed-out visitor to sign in for an admin row, refuses a signed-in non-admin, and lists only permitted rows on /x

interaction commerce-observation-provider-fact-price-observation-reaches-people
  source commerce-observation-provider
  destination fact-surface-registry
  relation produced_fact_to_public_surface
  preserves the records the producer wrote to the cms store, read as written, newest first, at most 50 rows and a total count
  drops columns the row does not name, cells past 240 bytes, rows past the limit and every write path
  forbidden_inference PriceObservation shown at /x/prices -> it is current, verified or the viewer may act on it
  invalidates_on the producer changing its table or columns, or the row's audience changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/fact_surfaces_test.sh
  binding schemas/control/fact-surfaces.cue
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/fact_surface_web.h

